1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,381
Double an angle, and
surely its sine doubles?

2
00:00:03,381 --> 00:00:05,483
Sine thirty degrees is one half.

3
00:00:05,883 --> 00:00:07,798
So sine sixty should be one.

4
00:00:07,798 --> 00:00:10,161
But it is zero point eight six six.

5
00:00:10,611 --> 00:00:13,730
Aarav spotted this while
doing homework at his desk.

6
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:18,650
Double again, to one twenty degrees,
and the sine does not grow at all.

7
00:00:19,150 --> 00:00:21,866
So what really happens
when you double an angle?

8
00:00:22,516 --> 00:00:28,319
Start from the sum formula: sin of x
plus y is sin x cos y plus cos x sin

9
00:00:28,319 --> 00:00:29,219
y.

10
00:00:29,201 --> 00:00:30,836
Put y equal to x.

11
00:00:30,836 --> 00:00:32,961
Then x plus y is two x.

12
00:00:33,711 --> 00:00:37,733
So sin two x is sin x
cos x plus cos x sin x.

13
00:00:37,733 --> 00:00:41,033
The same term twice: two sin x cos x.

14
00:00:41,783 --> 00:00:43,194
Here is the picture.

15
00:00:43,194 --> 00:00:47,400
An angle of two x at the centre,
between two radii of length one.

16
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:48,930
Join the ends.

17
00:00:48,930 --> 00:00:53,641
With one radius as base, the height
is sine two x, so the area is half

18
00:00:53,641 --> 00:00:54,831
of sine two x.

19
00:00:55,231 --> 00:00:59,835
Now cut it down the middle: two right
triangles, each with sides cos x

20
00:00:59,835 --> 00:01:00,768
and sin x.

21
00:01:01,168 --> 00:01:03,972
Each has area half of sin x cos x.

22
00:01:03,972 --> 00:01:06,044
Same triangle, same area.

23
00:01:06,044 --> 00:01:08,860
So sine two x is two sin x cos x.

24
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:10,586
Watch it live.

25
00:01:10,586 --> 00:01:15,123
The coral curve is sine two x, and
the dashed curve is two sine x.

26
00:01:15,523 --> 00:01:16,859
They split apart.

27
00:01:16,859 --> 00:01:20,859
But two sin x cos x stays on
the coral curve every time.

28
00:01:21,509 --> 00:01:22,691
Now cosine.

29
00:01:22,691 --> 00:01:29,113
Put y equal to x in cos of x plus y:
cos two x is cos squared x minus sin

30
00:01:29,113 --> 00:01:30,230
squared x.

31
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:36,102
Swap sin squared for one minus cos
squared, and cos two x is two cos squared

32
00:01:36,102 --> 00:01:37,177
x minus one.

33
00:01:37,927 --> 00:01:41,290
Swap the other way: one
minus two sin squared x.

34
00:01:41,290 --> 00:01:43,037
Three forms, one value.

35
00:01:43,787 --> 00:01:49,019
From the tan of a sum, tan two x is
two tan x over one minus tan squared

36
00:01:49,019 --> 00:01:49,919
x.

37
00:01:50,213 --> 00:01:55,005
Divide by cos squared plus sin squared,
which is one, and sine two x and

38
00:01:55,005 --> 00:01:57,982
cos two x can be written with tan x alone.

39
00:01:58,632 --> 00:01:59,891
Side by side.

40
00:01:59,891 --> 00:02:01,395
Know only cos x?

41
00:02:01,395 --> 00:02:04,041
Use two cos squared x minus one.

42
00:02:04,441 --> 00:02:05,902
Know only sin x?

43
00:02:05,902 --> 00:02:08,474
Use one minus two sin squared x.

44
00:02:09,074 --> 00:02:10,323
Pause and think.

45
00:02:10,323 --> 00:02:11,896
Sine x is one third.

46
00:02:11,896 --> 00:02:14,464
Which form of cos two x is quickest?

47
00:02:17,664 --> 00:02:22,439
One minus two sin squared x: one minus
two ninths, which is seven ninths.

48
00:02:23,089 --> 00:02:24,712
Now the triple angle.

49
00:02:24,712 --> 00:02:27,062
Write three x as two x plus x.

50
00:02:27,462 --> 00:02:28,474
Step one.

51
00:02:28,474 --> 00:02:33,103
Sin three x is sin two x
cos x plus cos two x sin x.

52
00:02:33,853 --> 00:02:34,753
Step two.

53
00:02:34,745 --> 00:02:39,683
Put in the double angle forms, then
change cos squared x into one minus

54
00:02:39,683 --> 00:02:40,912
sin squared x.

55
00:02:41,662 --> 00:02:42,680
Step three.

56
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:47,885
Collect the terms: sin three x is
three sin x minus four sin cubed x.

57
00:02:48,635 --> 00:02:53,738
The same way, cos three x is four
cos cubed x minus three cos x.

58
00:02:54,388 --> 00:02:55,368
Quick check.

59
00:02:55,368 --> 00:02:59,901
At thirty degrees, is sine of three
x equal to three times sine x?

60
00:02:59,901 --> 00:03:01,143
Pause and think.

61
00:03:04,343 --> 00:03:05,243
No!

62
00:03:04,826 --> 00:03:08,876
Three times sine thirty is
one point five, more than one.

63
00:03:08,876 --> 00:03:13,903
The formula gives one point five minus
zero point five: one, which is sine

64
00:03:13,903 --> 00:03:14,803
ninety.

65
00:03:15,245 --> 00:03:16,398
Remember this.

66
00:03:16,398 --> 00:03:19,382
Doubling the angle never doubles the sine.

67
00:03:19,382 --> 00:03:21,796
Sin two x is two sin x cos x.

68
00:03:22,496 --> 00:03:23,982
Now a worked example.

69
00:03:24,332 --> 00:03:27,408
Tan x is three quarters and x is acute.

70
00:03:27,408 --> 00:03:30,787
Find sin two x, cos two x and tan two x.

71
00:03:31,287 --> 00:03:32,187
Step one.

72
00:03:32,184 --> 00:03:37,366
A three four five triangle: sin x
is three fifths, cos x four fifths.

73
00:03:38,116 --> 00:03:39,016
Step two.

74
00:03:38,968 --> 00:03:43,683
Sin two x is two times three fifths
times four fifths: twenty four over

75
00:03:43,683 --> 00:03:44,690
twenty five.

76
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:46,450
Step three.

77
00:03:46,450 --> 00:03:51,475
Cos two x is sixteen twenty fifths
minus nine twenty fifths: seven twenty

78
00:03:51,475 --> 00:03:52,375
fifths.

79
00:03:52,950 --> 00:03:53,878
Step four.

80
00:03:53,878 --> 00:03:58,330
Tan two x is twenty four sevenths,
and the tan formula agrees.

81
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:00,445
Now, the exam trap.

82
00:04:00,795 --> 00:04:05,553
Many students flip the signs, and
write cos two x as one minus two cos

83
00:04:05,553 --> 00:04:06,463
squared x.

84
00:04:06,863 --> 00:04:08,558
Test at x equals zero.

85
00:04:08,558 --> 00:04:11,948
Cos zero is one, but that
form gives minus one.

86
00:04:11,948 --> 00:04:13,798
The right form gives one.

87
00:04:14,448 --> 00:04:16,175
Where is this asked?

88
00:04:16,175 --> 00:04:21,541
JEE Main, as in January twenty nineteen,
where a long product of cosines

89
00:04:21,541 --> 00:04:25,435
collapses using sin two
x equals two sin x cos x.

90
00:04:25,435 --> 00:04:27,104
And the PUC boards.

91
00:04:27,704 --> 00:04:29,099
Exam level now.

92
00:04:29,099 --> 00:04:30,446
Tan x is two.

93
00:04:30,446 --> 00:04:33,082
Find cos two x plus sin two x.

94
00:04:33,082 --> 00:04:34,535
Pause and solve.

95
00:04:39,935 --> 00:04:41,420
The answer is A.

96
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:42,422
One fifth.

97
00:04:42,922 --> 00:04:44,471
Use the tan forms.

98
00:04:44,471 --> 00:04:49,252
Sin two x is two tan x over one
plus tan squared: four fifths.

99
00:04:49,752 --> 00:04:54,990
Cos two x is one minus tan squared
over one plus tan squared: minus three

100
00:04:54,990 --> 00:04:55,890
fifths.

101
00:04:56,225 --> 00:04:57,125
Add them.

102
00:04:57,065 --> 00:05:00,067
Four fifths minus three
fifths is one fifth.

103
00:05:00,667 --> 00:05:02,126
Here is your recap.

104
00:05:02,126 --> 00:05:03,626
Screenshot this card.

105
00:05:06,826 --> 00:05:09,662
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

106
00:05:10,062 --> 00:05:10,962
One.

107
00:05:10,607 --> 00:05:13,437
Why is sine of two x not two sine x?

108
00:05:14,337 --> 00:05:15,237
Two.

109
00:05:14,895 --> 00:05:17,609
Write all three forms of cos two x.

110
00:05:18,509 --> 00:05:19,409
Three.

111
00:05:19,149 --> 00:05:22,294
If cos x is three fifths, find cos two x.

112
00:05:23,394 --> 00:05:27,995
Next time: two notes played together
make a beat, a sum hiding a product.

113
00:05:27,995 --> 00:05:29,234
Sums and products.
